\par\par \b \uc2  IMF hopes for deal on new Brazil funds this week. \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1999\par 17:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Feb 24 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund hopes to finish a deal with Brazil this week that will allow the resumption of payments under a $41.5 billion rescue deal, an IMF spokesman said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "We still hope that a deal can be reached this week," the spokesman said. He said no details would be available until the arrangement was finished and declined to comment on the latest actions by the authorities, including \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the fragile Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the world's eighth largest economy, turned to the IMF for help last year after crisis in Russia and other countries exposed its own financial weaknesses. \par \par \uc2  An international rescue package was approved in November and a first $5.3 billion payment handed over in December. \par \par \uc2  The IMF had initially expected to pay a second, $4.5 billion instalment of its loan to Brazil by the end of this month. But the plans were thrown into disarray after Brazil was forced to bow to market pressure and devalue the real. \par \par \uc2  The two sides have been negotiating terms for payments to restart for the last weeks. Growth and inflation forecasts will have to be revised and new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  guidelines set. \par \par \uc2  A Brazilian finance ministry official said demands from Brazilian states for debt relief should not affect the IMF talks, and the fund spokesman confirmed the IMF negotiated with the central government rather than with individual states. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry Executive Secretary Pedro Parente said the talks were making progress and only "two or three" technical questions remained unresolved. \par \par \uc2  He did not believe the IMF would wait for agreement to increase the CPMF financial transaction tax, expected to reach a final vote in March, before freeing the next tranche of aid. \par \par \uc2  ((Washington newsroom, +1 202 898 8309, washington.economic.newsroom@reuter)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2o03vom\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
