\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 /Money -2: Fraga Up Next \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1999\par 21:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  come just days before the nominee to head the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Arminio Fraga, is set to begin confirmation proceedings in the Senate. More concrete guidelines on the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy are expected to follow. \par \par \uc2  "Once Fraga is installed, the market might be less willing to speculate, which will stop (real-dollar) rates rising," said Warburg Dillon Read's Chicharo. \par \par \uc2  Fraga, who until his nomination was a fund manager with international financier George Soros, is well-respected for his market expertise. \par \par \uc2  Nobody can safely predict what the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new policy will be, but all agree the role of the International Monetary Fund - still in talks with Brazilian officials on revising the terms of last year's $41.5 billion credit line - will be fundamental. \par \par \uc2  "There won't be any immediate announcement on the new policy due to the ongoing negotiations with the IMF, but they (the IMF) will have a strong influence on it," said Leonardo Veras, fund manager for brokerage Graphus Participacoes in Rio. He did expect, however, some form of "dirty" float, possibly like Mexico's, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells a fixed $200 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market whenever the peso weakens by more than 2% in one trading session. \par \par \uc2  "This would have to be backed up by foreign credit lines," Veras added, explaining that this would help inject life into Brazil's spluttering financial markets. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the disbursement of the second IMF tranche for Brazil - thought to be around $9 billion - will be key to keeping the lid on bubbling market volatility. \par \par \uc2  Until then, real-dollar levels are unlikely to come down, inflation will mount, and the high interest rates - currently at 39% - required to try and control these pressures will increase the country's already bloated public debt. \par \par \uc2  The IMF and Brazil are reviewing the terms of the aid package precisely owing to the real's devaluation last month. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Nowhere in the world has a completely free-float \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, not\par even Japan," said Chicharo, who added that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will\par announce its new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rules, but might not disclose specific\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels to the market.\par -By Jamie McGeever; 5521-580-9394; jmcgeever@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-02-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2011GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1149 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2o01imo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
