\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 , Putting Money Where Mouth Is \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jamie McGeever \par \uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1999\par 20:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waded back into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time since it free-floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than a month ago, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for two days running to steady the real. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  began Tuesday when the real (BRR) weakened as far as BRR2.08 to the dollar, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell a small amount of dollars - around $30 million, according to market estimates - for the first time since the Jan. 18 free-float. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had come under heightened pressure because of settlements Friday of March dollar futures contracts. \par \par \uc2  And the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeated the action just before midsession Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hovered around BRR2.00/dlr. \par \par \uc2  Up until Tuesday, market speculation had it that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars through select financial agents, most notably the federally-run Banco do Brasil, although there was no official confirmation of activity. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it intends to control brusque \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, and on Tuesday and Wednesday spokespeople confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  while giving no further information on the sales. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday was extremely positive, as it showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's closely watching the market, and ready to correct price distortions," said Aline Chicharo, director of proprietary trading at Warburg Dillon Read in Rio de Janeiro. She said banks long on dollars might stop buying at Tuesday's high rates now that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has flexed its muscle, which could reduce the chances of a run on the real. \par \par \uc2  Jose Mauricio Haddock Lobo, head of fixed income sales at investment bank Fleming Graphus in Rio, also welcomed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pro-active return to the market. \par \par \uc2  "This gave the market parameters, and is also an incentive for exporters to enter the market again," Lobo said, pointing out that it's in exporters' interests to enter the exchange market when the dollar is at its strongest point. \par \par \uc2  Lobo said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while different from the sorts of formal dollar auctions held prior to the float, sent a signal to the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't hesitate to control price swings whenever it sees fit. \par \par \uc2  Prior to the free-float, the real traded against the dollar within a crawling band which was weakened slightly every two to five working days, resulting in a controlled depreciation of the real of around 7.5% a year. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 24-02-99 \par \par \uc2  1912GMT \par \par \uc2  1149 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2o01ija\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
