\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Mkt ADRs Inch Up As Investors Eye Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1999\par 17:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market shares trading as American depositary receipts Wednesday were mixed to higher in thin volumes as the market awaited news of Brazil's direction. \par \par \uc2  At around 1600 GMT, the Bank of New York index of Latin America ADRs was up 0.3% to 74.72. \par \par \uc2  "People are still very nervous, particularly in Brazil," said one trader. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is weakening, and they're not sure what to make of that." \par \par \uc2  Telebras HOLDRs remained remained unchanged at $66 3/16. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to halt the slide of the real for the first time since it floated its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the start of the year. Investors are also keeping a close eye on would-be \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Arminio Fraga's upcoming confirmation hearings in Congress, as well as continuing discussions over the CPMF tax levied on checks, cash withdrawals and transfers, which is a key part of the government's fiscal package. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Latin America, Chile's Enersis rose 2.8% to $25 3/16, ahead of a key vote by shareholders on a bylaw change that would allow the Spanish utility Endesa to proceed with a $1.4 billion tender offer for control of the company. Endesa-Chile, which is partly owned by Enersis and is currently the object of a $2.1 billion bid by Duke Energy, climbed 2.9% to $13 1/4. \par \par \uc2  Mexican and Argentine ADRs were mixed to higher in relatively small volumes. Mexico's Telefonos de Mexico gained 0.8% to $58 7/16, while Argentina's YPF gained 0.4% to $29 1/4. \par \par \uc2  Asian ADRs were strengthening Wednesday, albeit in razor-thin volumes, as many local bourses remained shuttered for the Lunar New Year. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea's SK Telecom added 0.6% to $10, following Moody's Investor\par Service's announcement that it had changed its outlook on the company's\par rating to stable from negative. Indonesia's PT Telekomunikasi,\par meanwhile, remained unchanged at $6 5/8.\par -By Thomas Catan; (201) 938-2225; thomas.catan@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-02-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1629GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1836 5076 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2o01i0l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
