\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil real firms 0.53 pct to close at 1.90/dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 1999\par 20:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Feb 12 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed 0.53 percent to close on Friday at an offer of 1.90 reais per dollar as trading wound down ahead of Carnival festivities, which begin this weekend, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, has now depreciated by 36.3 percent since the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to relax its stiff \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy on Jan. 13 in the face of massive dollar outflows. \par \par \uc2  "Some institutions entered right at the end, selling a few dollars," one trader said. Market participants said the volume of dollar sales was small and scattered, but sufficient to give the real a boost. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell back from an earlier high of 1.88 per dollar, reached amid talk that federal bank Banco do Brasil might be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But such an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to materialise. \par \par \uc2  Banco do Brasil, which has acted on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past, ended up selling a small amount of $15 million which could have been dollar sales on behalf of its clients, traders said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers have been anxiously watching for signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  named Arminio Fraga, a former aide to billionaire speculator George Soros, as the new president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((-Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248-5412)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2c04oyu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
