\par\par \b \uc2  Wall Street expects Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rules by Friday. \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1999\par 22:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Feb 3 (Reuters) - Wall Street analysts said they expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  to announce a new policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules by this Friday. \par \par \uc2  The policy will likely stipulate the minimum percentage move in the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The guidelines will also provide some detail on the mechanisms that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would use to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as use of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund and the U.S. Treasury do not in principal support \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but would go along with a well-defined and limited programme, said analysts who have talked with Brazilian officials. \par \par \uc2  Brazilians have examined the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  system now in place in Mexico but the Brazilian version will be different, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Mexico's current policy allows an infusion of dollars into the market through an auction process if the peso drops more than five percent in one day. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "could use some type of options to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets ... or some other mechanism while holding to some inflation target," said John Welch, chief Latin American economist at Paribas. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's President Fernando Henrique Cardoso said Wednesday that any new exchange rate policy would steer clear of any type of "band" to contain the movement of the real. \par \par \uc2  The Cardoso government is in negotiations with the International Monetary Fund on resetting monetary and fiscal targets after Brazil allowed the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to float last month. \par \par \uc2  The shift in the exchange rate policy triggered a series of changes at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday, Arminio Fraga, former aide to international financier George Soros, was appointed president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He succeeds Francisco Lopes, who held the job for three weeks after Gustavo Franco, staunch proponent of a strong real, resigned as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief. \par \par \uc2  ((-Apu Sikri; N.A. Treasury Desk; 212 859-1562 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2305320\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
