\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Brazil turns to Soros aide amid crisis. \b0\par\par\uc2  By William Schomberg \par \uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1999\par 23:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, Feb 2 (Reuters) - Crisis-torn Brazil stunned markets again on Tuesday when it named its second \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president in three weeks, entrusting its giant but ailing economy to an aide of billionaire speculator George Soros. \par \par \uc2  Arminio Fraga, a former \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director and until now managing director of Soros' powerful investment fund, rushed from New York to the Finance Ministry in Brasilia, where the International Monetary Fund and local officials were searching for ways to avoid a Russia-style collapse in Brazil. \par \par \uc2  The battered real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wobbled on the surprise appointment but staged a healthy recovery, closing at 1.75 to the dollar. That was its strongest level in more than a week, though it was still down 31 percent since Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis erupted on Jan 13. \par \par \uc2  Also helping the real on Tuesday were new rules making it easier for banks to sell dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Economists said Fraga, 42, was a brilliant thinker who would bring priceless experience of working in volatile markets to the government as it scrambled keep a grip on the real and a lid on inflation amid Brazil's worst financial crisis in decades. \par \par \uc2  "International investors are going to take this news very positively," said Walter Molano, head of research at BCP Securities in Greenwich, Conn. "Arminio Fraga is very well known, prominent and he has credibility among international economists." \par \par \uc2  Some Brazilians worried about Fraga's links to Soros, whose activities have been linked in the past to other countries' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  problems. \par \par \uc2  "The speculators were so successful in their attack on our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that they not only devalued the real but they've taken over the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Workers Party lawmaker and left-wing economist Aloisio Mercadante. \par \par \uc2  But Mercadante conceded Fraga would probably manage to stabilise Brazil's newly floated real, an essential first step before the government can cut soaring interest rates to ease a looming recession and reduce the threat of a debt default. \par \par \uc2  Soros on Monday criticised Brazil's recent hike in rates to nearly 40 percent a year, calling it a "disastrous move" that increased the risk of a devastating debt default. \par \par \uc2  But people who know Fraga said he would have his own ideas on how the world's eighth-biggest economy should be run. \par \par \uc2  "You shouldn't confuse George Soros with Arminio Fraga," said Paulo Leme, director of emerging markets at Goldman Sachs in New York. "He has independent ideas that sometimes may coincide with those of Soros but at other times differ radically." \par \par \uc2  Fraga's name had been mentioned as a possible adviser to President Fernando Henrique Cardoso, but his nomination to run the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  caught the country by surprise. \par \par \uc2  Only last week the Senate confirmed Francisco Lopes as president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the resignation of Gustavo Franco, a key economic policy-maker, on Jan. 13. That was when Brazil tried to stage a controlled devaluation, only to be forced by the markets to float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  two days later. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Pedro Malan told reporters on Tuesday he had submitted his own resignation during the crisis but that the president had insisted he stay on. \par \par \uc2  "I will remain in the position as long as I have the benefit of the president's confidence," he said. \par \par \uc2  Both Malan and Cardoso have been criticised for going back on pledges not to devalue the real. The president - reelected with a huge majority in October - has seen his ratings plunge to new lows in recent opinion polls. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the arrival of Fraga might help restore some of Brazil's battered credibility in international markets. \par \par \uc2  Lopes was considered a text-book economist but quickly lost face after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refused to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week, allowing the real to plunge to 2.18 to the dollar on Friday, when many Brazilians rushed to the banks to pull out their savings. \par \par \uc2  The powerful president of the Senate - which has to approve the nomination - gave Fraga his all-important blessing shortly after the news broke. \par \par \uc2  "I have known Dr. Arminio Fraga for a long time and I can say that he is extremely competent," Antonio Carlos Magalhaes, a political ally of Cardoso, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Before running the massive portfolio \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Soros Fund Management investment fund, Fraga was international affairs director at Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 1991 and 1992 and was involved in negotiations with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  One of Fraga's first tasks may be to hammer out an agreement with the IMF over the release of a second $9 billion tranche of international loans to see Brazil through its crisis. \par \par \uc2  Brazil agreed in November to fiscal and monetary targets in return for a $41.5 billion loan package from the IMF, other international lenders and top industrial nations. \par \par \uc2  However, the higher cost of Brazil's massive debt mountain resulting from the devaluation has dashed any chance the government had of meeting the targets, which are now being revised. \par \par \uc2  The talks in Brasilia were also focused on new ways for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to protect the real against the kind of wild fluctuations seen last week. \par \par \uc2  IMF First Deputy Managing Director Stanley Fischer arrived in Brazil late on Monday to speed up the negotiations. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv220580b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
