\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Cenbank to stop releasing daily  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  flows. \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1999\par 23:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, Jan 29 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it will stop releasing daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market flows and begin publishing reserves levels every day to avoid misinterpretations about the country's reserves. \par \par \uc2  "In the last few days, the outflows in the commercial and floating market based on information in the Sisbacen (\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  computerized information system), were wrongly interpreted as a loss in reserves," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said this interpretation is "obviously inadequate" in a free-float exchange regime, in which the only loss in reserves takes place when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sends money abroad or sells dollars in the market. \par \par \uc2  "Except for this situation, all information about the demand and supply of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market is completely reflected in the exchange rate," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement said. \par \par \uc2  Brazil abandoned its crawling peg system on Jan. 13 by attempting a controlled 8 percent devaluation, but two days later, it was forced to float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said it would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally. Under the old regime, it had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently to defend the peg. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost a net $8.385 billion through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets so far this month, after a net $5.16 billion was pulled out in December. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5537)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1t05ilc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
