\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank \highlight\uc2 /Reserves -2: No Plans To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 1999\par 16:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves are "steady," as a result of no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the real, a top official said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign affairs director, Demosthenes Madureira de Pinho Neto, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the real will continue to float freely against the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially adopted a policy allowing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to float freely against the dollar on Jan. 18. \par \par \uc2  Pinho Neto also pointed out the difference between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows, which have reached over $8.2 billion, and losses in reserves. \par \par \uc2  "The two are not the same and the impression sometimes created is that the recent outflows are in fact from the country's reserves," he said. "That's not the case, and reserves are absolutely steady." \par \par \uc2  Pinho Neto didn't say at what level reserves stood at Thursday, but earlier this week new central banker Francisco Lopes said at his senate confirmation hearing that Brazil's reserves amounted to $36 billion. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1538GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1s00rmc\par }\