\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Brazil real drops despite interest rate hike. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Noriko Yamaguchi \par \uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1999\par 18:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Jan 27 (Reuters) - Brazil's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was edging toward a new low on Wednesday after an early morning interest rate hike by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to appease nervous market players, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The sagging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was offered at 1.90 to the dollar when traders broke for lunch - trading 3 percent weaker from its Tuesday close. It was down 36 percent since the government first relaxed its stiff \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy on January 13. \par \par \uc2  The level was a new low for the real. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been setting new troughs every day since the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  floated the fortress-like \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on January 15, two days after a failed attempt at a controlled devaluation. \par \par \uc2  "Honestly, we don't have any sense of direction," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst in Rio de Janeiro. "I'm not making new predictions after my stabilisation theory of 1.7 reais to the dollar became outdated quite some time ago." \par \par \uc2  The real's weakness on Wednesday came despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's initiative to set benchmark overnight market interest rates at 35.5 percent, up from Tuesday's 32.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Market players said that by raising interest rates, the Bank was encouraging investors to keep money in the fixed-income market and prevent a further wave of dollar outflows. That would take pressure off the real. \par \par \uc2  Brazil lost a net $541 million through its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Tuesday, a bigger-than-expected dollar flight. More than $8 billion has been pulled out of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in January alone. \par \par \uc2  An ongoing wave of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows has eaten away at Brazil's international reserves, now estimated at around a net $28 billion, excluding the financial aid package Brazil has received from the International Monetary Fund and other rich lenders. \par \par \uc2  Traders and economists said Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move did little to calm \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and even raised more doubts about Brazil's ability to meet its huge debt obligations. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates will have a negative effect on Brazil's burgeoning fiscal deficit, as 60 percent of the debt is now linked to the overnight rate. \par \par \uc2  "We're in a vicious cycle," said the Rio analyst. "The government wants to contain capital flight with higher interest rates, but that just makes it tough for the government, especially when people are still worried whether Brazil can pay its debts." \par \par \uc2  Odair Abate, chief economist at Lloyds Bank in Sao Paulo, said \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be prepared to "lose its foreign reserves and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market", as a transition cost after it floated the real. \par \par \uc2  "The outflows are not stopping because exporters are not in the market, fearing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could devalue more," said Abate. Export revenues, had they entered, would offset dollar outflows. \par \par \uc2  Abate said that by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would indicate an appropriate real/dollar level at least for the short term. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5423, noriko.yamaguchi@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1r05p38\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
