\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Stronger -2: No  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Soon \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 1999\par 19:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real (BRR) strengthened significantly against the dollar in mid-afternoon trading Tuesday, as players sold dollars traded on the commercial market to snap up cheap February dollar futures contracts expiring in three days, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 1735 GMT, the real was trading at a mid rate of BRR1.8050 per dollar on a spread of BRR1.78-1.83 per dollar, compared to the previous BRR1.9050 per dollar on a spread of BRR1.90-1.91 per dollar before the midsession break. The opening quote Tuesday was BRR1.79 per dollar, unchanged from Monday's end. \par \par \uc2  "The market is selling the commercial (dollar) and making nice arbitrage \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on February (dollar) futures," said a Rio de Janeiro dealer, referring to the technique of spotting a price discrepancy between two securities, and then taking advantage of it to make a quick profit. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders reported that the price of February contracts, which mature on January 29, was standing at BRR1.740. \par \par \uc2  "This is the free float market," said another Rio dealer. "Sometimes (real-dollar) prices go up, and rarely, they go down," he quipped. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said there had been no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - either directly or via its financial agent the Banco do Brasil - to ease the selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  On confirming the new free float exchange regime January 18, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to contain "brusque" movements in exchange rates. Traders consider this policy a "dirty float". \par \par \uc2  Since the new policy was unveiled, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made no official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday's Ptax, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  daily average on which all forward\par contacts are based, registered BRR1.7602 per dollar.\par    -By Jamie McGeever (5521) 580-9394; jmcgeever@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Corrected 1823GMT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-01-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1810GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1q00ncf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
