\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Intraday Real Appears To Steady Around BRR1.72/Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1999\par 15:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real (BRR) appeared to be steadying a little above 1.70 to the dollar in illiquid late morning trade Friday, a shade weaker from the previous session's close. \par \par \uc2  The late morning lull followed a volatile start to trading that included dealers' reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease strong selling pressure just after the opening. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined comment on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1410 GMT, the real was quoted at a mid rate of BRR1.72/dollar on a spread of BRR1.71-1.73/dlr, slightly weaker than BRR1.71/dlr on a spread of BRR1.70-1.72/dlr about an hour earlier. \par \par \uc2  The real had strengthened briefly to BRR1.6650/dlr amid dealers' reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through federally run Banco do Brasil. The abrupt change came after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened sharply weaker at BRR1.75/dlr, after ending Thursday at BRR1.6950/dlr. \par \par \uc2  "Things are slightly calmer now, but the market will probably test another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at BRR1.75/dlr later (in trading)," said a Rio de Janeiro dealer, citing the price the market feels \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set as a limit before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said it was difficult to say how many dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold to halt the real's slide against the dollar, but two ventured an estimate at around $100-$150 million, considered "reasonable", given market illiquidity. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 22-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1444GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1m00lyl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
