\par\par \b \uc2  CSCE coffee futures end weaker, in mid-range. \b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1999\par 22:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 22 (Reuters) - CSCE arabica coffee futures ended slightly lower on Friday, with prices finally settling in mid-range, after speculators played both sides of the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The main players were specs," said one trader. "The specs sold it and the specs bought it back." \par \par \uc2  Benchmark March coffee fell 0.50 cent a lb, to settle at 105.50 cents, after ranging between 107.00 and 104.00 cents, its lowest level in 12 weeks. \par \par \uc2  Second-month May ended 0.70 cent weaker, at 107.60 cents, while the rest of the board closed down 0.60 to 1.00 cent. \par \par \uc2  The March/May contango finished at 2.10 cents, compared with 2.30 cents at the close on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said economic turmoil in Brazil continued to keep the coffee market on the defensive. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time since it free-floated the real, defending the embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from engaging in a freefall. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real has depreciated some 30 percent since January 13, when the government devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before allowing it to float freely two days later. \par \par \uc2  Some traders feared the world's largest producer of coffee would cash in on the higher local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings from dollar-denominated exports and flood the market with coffee. \par \par \uc2  Since January 13, the March contract has lost 14.80 cents or more than 12 percent. \par \par \uc2  However, traders noted that March coffee has barely moved during the last three sessions, easing a little over a penny in heavy volumes. \par \par \uc2  "I think the selling has just been absorbed by roaster buying," said Merrill Lynch analyst Judith Ganes. "But if roasters have done all this pricing and buying, what happens next? I don't think it bodes well for coffee." \par \par \uc2  Some traders said increased shipments of coffee from Mexico and Central America is also likely to keep prices under pressure. In addition, they expected cheaper differentials for their coffee will draw more coffee to the board. \par \par \uc2  "Differentials are down and people are buying coffee at differentials they can tender it, so you're going to see a lot of coffee come to the board," said one physical trader, adding, "I don't see roasters bending over backward to buy coffee from us." \par \par \uc2  Other traders, however, said the market was oversold and due for a correction. They reckoned the funds had substantially reduced their net long position from the 11,227 lots reported as of January 12. \par \par \uc2  In addition, prospects for a sharply reduced 1999-2000 crop from Brazil following this season's bumper crop of 35-36 million bags was likely to underpin the market, they said. \par \par \uc2  Technically, traders pegged March support at 104.00-103.00 cents, with key psychological support noted at 100.00 cents. Resistance was seen at 107.00 cents, then 108.50-109.00 cents, they said. \par \par \uc2  After Friday's close, CSCE reported certified coffee stocks fell by 250 bags as of January 21, to 96,961 60-kg bags. There were 5,502 bags pending grading, the exchange said. \par \par \uc2  CSCE also reported 7,000 bags of coffee were graded and 1,750 bags passed exchange approval. \par \par \uc2  Total volume reached an estimated 15,024 lots. \par \par \uc2  CSCE is a subsidiary of the New York Board of Trade. \par \par \uc2  ((-Patricia Avidan, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640, patricia.avidan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1m064y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
