\par\par \b \uc2  CSCE coffee futures called to open up 1.00 cent. \b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1999\par 15:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2     NEW YORK, Jan 22 (Reuters) - CSCE arabica coffee futures were called to \par \par \uc2  open 1.00 cent higher Friday on the heels of overnight gains in London, \par \par \uc2  traders said. \par \par \uc2      Robusta futures in London rose on industry buying. Active March was up \par \par \uc2  $18 at the midday break at $1,714, ranging $1,722 to $1,695. \par \par \uc2      But some CSCE traders said the market was likely to come in closer to \par \par \uc2  unchanged, as bearish sentiment lingered following Thursday's close toward \par \par \uc2  intra-day lows. \par \par \uc2      "We're calling New York higher on London," said one trader. "But the \par \par \uc2  market still looks a little weak." \par \par \uc2     On Thursday, New York coffee ended mixed, with the nearby contracts \par \par \uc2  shedding early gains and posting modest losses. March fell 0.55 cent, to \par \par \uc2  settle at the day's low of 106.00 cents. March posted a high of 108.60 \par \par \uc2  cents. Second-month May eased 0.20 cent, to 108.30 cents, while the rest of \par \par \uc2  the board closed down 0.20 to up 0.75 cent. \par \par \uc2      The March/May contango finished at 2.30 cents, compared with 1.95 cents \par \par \uc2  at the close on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      Traders said uncertainty about the economic situation continued to \par \par \uc2  damped sentiment on Thursday. Brazil's real fell 7.6 percent on Thursday to \par \par \uc2  an all-time low of 1.72 per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2      On Friday, Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  was selling the U.S. dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through the \par \par \uc2  government-owned Banco do Brasil in order to rescue the real from a \par \par \uc2  precipitous fall that sparked fears of knock-on devaluations from Latin \par \par \uc2  America to Asia. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the world's largest producer and exporter of coffee. \par \par \uc2      Technically, traders pegged March resistance at 107.50 cents, then \par \par \uc2  109.00 cents. Support was seen at 106.00-105.00 cents, followed by 103.00 \par \par \uc2  cents. \par \par \uc2      After Thursday's close, CSCE reported certified coffee stocks rose \par \par \uc2  2,250 bags as of January 20, at 97,211 60-kg bags. There were 12,502 bags \par \par \uc2  pending grading, the exchange said. \par \par \uc2      CSCE is a subsidiary of the New York Board of Trade. \par \par \uc2     ((-- Patricia Avidan, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640, \par \par \uc2  patricia.avidan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1m05x2e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
