\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  c.bank says will not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mkt. \b0\par\par\uc2 190 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1999\par 16:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, Jan 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated Thursday morning that it will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to impede sharp fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate will be set by the market in function of dollar flows, Altamir Lopes, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic department, said. \par \par \uc2  "There is no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I am unaware of any intention in that respect," Lopes told a monthly news conference to release current account data. \par \par \uc2  The real sank to a new low of 1.72 to the dollar in late morning trading Thursday, taking its devaluation since last Tuesday to nearly 30 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed the fall to a shortage of dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision Friday not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to protect the real. The shortage has been aggravated by steady dollar outflows since then. \par \par \uc2  "The market has fluctuated as a result of the daily (dollar) flows," Lopes said. \par \par \uc2  ((-Brasilia newsroom 5561 314 1193; raquel.stenzel@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \