\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Malan -3: No Specific  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Point For Real \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 1999\par 17:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Exiting the talks, Malan said he had "no comment on the appropriate level of the real," adding that the government hadn't set any specific point at which to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He added that there has been no discussion of restructuring Brazil's mounting debt, saying "We are not going to have any domestic debt restructuring." \par \par \uc2  On the fiscal front, Malan said he expected congress to vote on and approve social security reform Wednesday, calling it a "very important vote." \par \par \uc2  International investors have been watching Brazil closely for signs that it will carry out the reforms required under its $41.5 billion rescue from the International Monetary Fund. That includes passage by congress of the necessary reforms to the pension system. \par \par \uc2  Finally, Malan said the bankers gathered Wednesday in New York didn't discuss any alternative to the new free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime for the real. \par \par \uc2  "The issue of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board was raised over the last several months in Brazil," Malan said. "We explained why we don't think it is an appropriate exchange regime for Brazil." \par \par \uc2  Brazil was thrown into crisis after the state of Minas Gerais earlier this month declared a moratorium on payment of its debts to the federal government. The resultant outflow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced Brazil to effectively devalue the real by widening the band in which the real is allowed to trade. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The real rallied Tuesday after Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised interest\par rates, closing at 1.56 reals per dollar, up from 1.59 reals per dollar\par at Monday's close. It was slightly weaker at midday Wednesday at 1.5755\par reals per dollar.\par    By Thomas Catan; 201-938-2225\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-01-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1603GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1k00go0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
