\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Brazil will honor debts, finmin tells bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Apu Sikri \par \uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 1999\par 18:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 20 (Reuters) - Brazil will honour all loan obligations and do its best to contain a domestic financial crisis that has threatened global financial stability, Finance Minister Pedro Malan told a dozen top bankers on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "We are not going to have any domestic debt restructuring," Malan told reporters after meeting with U.S. banking leaders at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. \par \par \uc2  Brazil owes international banks about $70 billion in short-term debt, according to bankers, and another $300 billion to domestic financial institutions. Economists have questioned the Latin American giant's ability to meet its obligations. \par \par \uc2  Malan on Wednesday assured bankers - including Goldman Sachs co-chairman Jon Corzine, Merrill Lynch chief executive David Komansky and financier George Soros - that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. \par \par \uc2  Malan called the meeting "constructive." Brazil hopes to win back investor confidence after a decision last Friday to float the real - a move that will help the country preserve precious \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  "It is up to the markets to decide what is the appropriate exchange rate. We do not have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  points, virtual bands, notional bands. And we do not have a hidden agenda," Malan told reporters after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Brazil has also ruled out adoption of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board - which would link the value of the real to the dollar and take away most decision-making from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Malan said. \par \par \uc2  "We have decided on a floating exchange rate regime and this is the regime we are going to have," Malan said. "This is not a criticism of any country that adopts the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board scheme." \par \par \uc2  Brazil's neighbour Argentina has implemented a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board deemed successful by most economists. \par \par \uc2  The real has lost more than a quarter of its value against the dollar since last week's devaluation and subsequent abandoning of exchange rate bands. \par \par \uc2  Bankers have privately asserted that Brazil needs the support of private lenders to avoid a debt default of the sort that trapped Russia last year and set off panic in financial markets. \par \par \uc2  Official lenders led by the International Monetary Fund and the United States arranged $41.5 billion in loans to Brazil late last year to contain financial turmoil that threatened to infect Latin America and other regions. \par \par \uc2  Malan was accompanied by Secretary of Economic Policy Amaury Bier and International Affairs Secretary Marcos Caramuru. \par \par \uc2  ((-N.A. Treasury Desk; 212 859-1562 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1k0688k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
