\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil seeks IMF, U.S. backing in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  crisis. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anthony Boadle \par \uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 1999\par 06:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Jan 17 (Reuters) - Brazilian Finance Minister Pedro Malan will meet U.S. officials on Sunday seeking their endorsement of a shock decision to allow Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, to devalue. \par \par \uc2  Malan was due to meet Deputy U.S. Treasury Secretary Larry Summers on Sunday, after meeting with International Monetary Fund Managing Director Michel Camdessus on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  An aide to Malan said they discussed Friday's decision to give in to market pressure and let Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely and the impact the devaluation will have on the world's eighth-largest economy. \par \par \uc2  "Brazil came to explain and try to obtain support for the changes made this week," the aide told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  He said the talks also covered the impact a devalued real will have on Brazil's economic programme with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  That programme was agreed to in November as part of a $41.5 billion international rescue plan by rich industrial nations to save Brazil from following Russia into a financial maelstrom. \par \par \uc2  The plan had succeeded in bolstering confidence in the real until the governor of Brazil's third-largest state, Minas Gerais, spooked investors by declaring a 90-day moratorium on debt payments to the federal government. \par \par \uc2  Faced with a renewed run on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Brazil tried a controlled devaluation on Wednesday and on Friday stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the real, the pillar of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic stability since 1994. \par \par \uc2  The real fell as low as 1.55 to the dollar, but then stabilised at around 1.42 to the dollar, down some 15 percent in value in the week. \par \par \uc2  Dollar outflows from Brazil slowed on Friday and shares soared 33 percent on the Sao Paulo stock market as investors saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not tumble out of control. \par \par \uc2  "You saw what happened. There was no big run," Malan told reporters on arrival in Washington. "The market set the value and it was a stronger level than some people had expected." \par \par \uc2  "It was a positive step," he said. \par \par \uc2  Malan, who was accompanied by newly-appointed \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Francisco Lopes, said the bank will announce new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rules on Monday in Brasilia. \par \par \uc2  The alternatives range from a permanently floating rate to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board like the one Argentina adopted successfully in 1991 - a rigid regime that pegs the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmly one-to-one to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A middle road is a new rate loosely pegged to the dollar like the one abandoned on Friday, but with wider ranges for the real to fluctuate in. \par \par \uc2  The decision to float the real essentially scrapped the cornerstone of the Real Plan, which based itself on a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to successfully tame hyperinflation in Brazil. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Brazil will have to move faster now to put its public accounts in order by passing fiscal reforms that were delayed in Congress. \par \par \uc2  They said Brazil does not need to ask for more funds from the IMF and the Group of Seven rich nations, because it has hardly used any of the $41.5 billion loan package. \par \par \uc2  But they stressed that Brazil must enact promised reforms to cut its huge fiscal deficit if it wants markets to maintain confidence in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Malan's aide said the Brazilian government may ask the IMF to speed up the second disbursement from the international rescue package, some $4.5 billion due at the end of February. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said in December it was prepared to pay out this money sooner if Brazil requested it. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1h06hxz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
