\par\par \b \uc2  =S&P: Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Move Ups Risk, But No More Downgrades Seen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Angela Pruitt \par \uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 19:51\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Standard & Poor's said Friday's decision by Brazil to temporarily allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, to float heightened the risk level for the country. \par \par \uc2  But the ratings agency said it would not immediately further downgrade Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ratings. \par \par \uc2  Emerging markets were sent in yet another tailspin Thursday, partly because S&P downgraded Brazil's long-term foreign and local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ratings to single-B-plus and double-B-minus, from double-B-minus and double-B-plus, respectively. \par \par \uc2  "The downgrade had already factored in a strong possibility that the exchange policy will be changed again and that the real will float. This event, in and of itself, is not unexpected," said Lacy Gallagher, director of S&P's sovereign ratings group. She was referring to the announcement by Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday that it was revoking a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of BRR1.20-BRR1.32 set Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  By letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float, Brazil's interest rates will remain higher and the country's gross domestic product will contract more than the 1% projected in the IMF program, said Gallagher. \par \par \uc2  She also noted that continued fiscal discipline and expedient passage of the remaining measures of Brazil's $23 billion economic reform plan would be key to Brazil's credit worthiness. The reform program, which includes spending cuts and tax hikes, was agreed to with the International Monetary Fund as part of a $41.5 billion IMF-led bailout for Brazil unveiled in November. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it wouldn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday and would issue a statement on its\par exchange rate regime on Monday.\par -By Angela Pruitt; 201-938-2269\par angela.pruitt@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  15-01-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1851GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010827dv1f000nm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
