\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Stages Surprise Rally After Brazil Float \b0\par\par\uc2  By Marianne Sullivan \par \uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 22:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar surprised many in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday, rallying against the yen and euro, when most thought it should plunge following Brazil's float of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. \par \par \uc2  Brazil has long been considered to hold the key of contagion for the spread of the global economic crisis. As Brazil is the world's 11th largest economy, many believed the country's collapse would present a sizable risk to regional and U.S. markets and their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But after \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would no longer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the real, markets experienced what traders called a relief rally. \par \par \uc2  "It's surprising and counter-intuitive," said Andrew Chaveriat, technical analyst at Paribas in New York. "We thought the dollar and U.S. and Brazilian stocks would get slammed. We thought there would be more capital flight. Instead, in emerging markets, people are buying everything in sight." \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the dollar rallied to an intraday high of Y114.19 around midday in New York and the euro had fallen to an intraday low of $1.5566 three hours later, from Y112.68 and $1.636 before news of the float. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's Bovespa stock index rose 33.5%; Mexico's IPC index closed up 6.66% and the Dow Jones Industrial Average finished 219.62 points higher. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's real, which traded as high as BRR1.5500 per dollar after the float, was quoted late Friday at BRR1.4200 per dollar. The Mexican peso closed sharply stronger at MXN10.2200 to the dollar. Other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and markets also joined the rally. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York Friday, the dollar was trading at Y113.81, up from Y113.61 late Thursday and the euro was trading at $1.1567, down from $1.1700 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 15-01-99 \par \par \uc2  2138GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1f00dc1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
