\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar ends easier in Asia, softer bias seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 11:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Jan 15 (Reuters) - The dollar ended a quiet Asian session weaker amid continued worries over the financial situation in Brazil, traders and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 112.78/88 yen at 0730 GMT compared with its New York close of 113.75/85. The euro was trading at US$1.1720/30, firmer than its U.S. close of 1.1690/95. \par \par \uc2  Activity was light with Tokyo on holiday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had a soft tone and would continue under pressure until Brazil's future became more clear, sources said. \par \par \uc2  Brazilian traders said about US$1 billion flooded out of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the third day in a row on Thursday, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars from its falling reserves and keep the real within its new, lower band. \par \par \uc2  Brazil devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The situation put pressure on the dollar amid fears that the United States, which has major trade flows with Latin America, would be particularly hurt if the Brazilian crisis became a regional one. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is still susceptible to downside risk against the majors, probably more so against the euro, the Swiss franc and sterling and less so against the yen," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at a Hong Kong bank. \par \par \uc2  "The lesser weakness against the yen is partly due to Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but also to the idea that if \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  goes there may be some contagion in Asia," he said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ engaged in dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week to stem the rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar was likely to come under further selling pressure in Europe and the U.S. because few traders would want to hold long dollar positions over a three-day weekend in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  U.S. markets will be closed Monday for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  "I think the euro will test around the 1.1750/80 level," said a trader at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  "But I think the euro is toppish overall and I would sell it at 1.1780," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrea Ricci (852) 2568-6773; Fax (852) 2845-0636; hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1f06fir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
