\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Tsys Dn Late; Reverse Flight-To-Quality Bid; 30Y -1 Pt \b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1999\par 21:00\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--U.S. Treasurys were trading down, but off intraday lows, late Friday, capping a shortened session of intense volatility fueled by the unexpected, dramatic rally in Brazilian stocks which underpinned neighboring U.S. equity markets. \par \par \uc2  At 2:47 p.m. EST, the benchmark 30-year bond was down one point at 101 30/32 to yield 5.12%. At the Chicago Board of Trade, the March bond contract settled at 126-17, down 24/32. Bond markets observed an early close. \par \par \uc2  The Sao Paulo Bovespa stock index soared as high as 30% by afternoon New York trading, following the session's free float of the Brazilian real. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday - two days after the government widened the real's trading band against the dollar that effectively devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 8%. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average was trading about 157 points higher by 2:57 p.m. EST. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that financial markets have known the value of the real would fall, but the uncertainty was when. The move by Brazil to let the real go this week was seen as removing some of that uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  Treasurys fell as the flight-to-quality bid reversed out of the market, but managed to find support near yields of 5.12% in the long bond. In the shift out of bonds and into stocks, traders said that market participants were also squaring up their positions going into the three-day weekend. U.S. financial markets will be closed Monday to observe Martin Luther King Day. \par \par \uc2  "Basically, investors realize that after they float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  where people are comfortable, buying (Brazilian assets) can recommence," said Richard Gilhooly, bond market strategist at Paribas Capital Markets in New York. "Whether or not this is sustainable is another matter." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indeed, some market participants were skeptical of Friday's bullish\par reaction in stocks and the safe-haven withdrawal in Treasurys. Brazil's\par finance minister Pedro Malan and newly-appointed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  president\par Francisco Lopes will both meet with International Monetary Fund\par officials over the weekend in Washington, D.C., and a statement is\par expected from the Brazilian government Monday on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policy.\par    4 5/8    2-year     100  4/32  dn  6/32  4.56%\par    4 1/4%   5-year      98 23/32  dn 12/32  4.55%\par    4 3/4%  10-year     100 17/32  dn 18/32  4.68%\par    5 1/4%  30-year     101 30/32  dn 32/32  5.12%\par    2-30-yr yield spread: 56 BPS vs 61 BPS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  01-15-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1500EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1079 20715 4041 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dv1f003eo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
