\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Policy -2: Real Pressured, Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 16:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although he said the move wasn't drastic, Lopes said that the new band will serve as a transition to a floating exchange rate policy. He didn't, however, provide a time frame for a shift to a new policy. \par \par \uc2  "With the changes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in reality speeding up a process which had been occurring in a gradual manner," Lopes said. \par \par \uc2  The attempt to fiddle with policy in the middle of the storm didn't go over well with markets anywhere. \par \par \uc2  In Brazil, the real immediately popped past the new outer limit of the band. \par \par \uc2  The real moved as weak as BRR1.33 to the dollar by early afternoon, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to confirm the levels at which it held its dollar auction, although traders reported it was at the official ceiling of BRR1.3200. \par \par \uc2  By 1520 GMT, the real was trading at BRR1.3210. \par \par \uc2  Walter Stoeppelwerth, head of research at Flemings in Sao Paulo, noted that Lopes in the past has espoused having an even wider band during the transitional phase prior to the full float. Stoeppelwerth said he wouldn't be surprised to see a band of BRR1.30-BRR1.70 or BRR1.35-BRR1.70 in the near future. \par \par \uc2  "Our sense is that this is a baby step. They're effectively on the edge of the abyss," Stoeppelwerth said. "I think it's a not very effective attempt to buy some time." \par \par \uc2  The key to the longevity of the new policy is, of course, how quickly investors leave Brazil and how much the country is willing to spend to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As of Wednesday, the country had just over $31 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - in addition to a $41.5-billion International Monetary Fund package. On Tuesday, Brazil suffered a massive $1.2 billion capital outflow. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1555GMT \par \par \uc2  1191 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1d00a86\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
