\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's real stable as  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mkts lose $500 mln. \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 1998\par 21:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Oct 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed stable Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling dollars to offset capital flight of about $500 million from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , via federally owned Banco do Brasil, sold dollars, bolstering a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the speculation. \par \par \uc2  The real closed unchanged at 1.19 to the dollar in the commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  About $500 million fled the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday, according to traders' preliminary estimates. If the amount is confirmed, it will mark the biggest day of dollar flight in more than a week. \par \par \uc2  Some $30 billion fled Brazil in August and September. A sharp hike in interest rates slowed outflows and spurts of foreign direct investment in October enabled Brazil to register a net dollar inflow so far this month. \par \par \uc2  Still, more money could leave as foreign loans and bonds come due and as investors await confirmation of an international loan to Brazil. \par \par \uc2  As of 1700 local/1900 gmt a net $250 million were registered leaving Brazil through the commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, while another $79 million had left through the floating \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed unchanged at 1.1921 reais to the dollar in the floating market and stable at 1.285 to the dollar in the parallel market. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5408)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duam02efx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
