\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Outflows Wane \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1998\par 22:56\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real (BRL) weakened against the dollar Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the crawling band in which the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  The trading session, however, was marked by a positive tone as the bleeding of dollars seemed to diminish considerably. \par \par \uc2  At 1950 GMT, preliminary \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures showed an outflow of $272 million via the commercial exchange market and $100 million via the floating-rate market. \par \par \uc2  Market participants told Dow Jones Newswires they estimated the two markets would post a total outflow of $700 million Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The apparent slowdown in outflows comes after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday restricted credit for banks, which effectively boosted domestic interest rates to around 29.75% from 19% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Still, the real weakened in the spot market, where the commercial dollar for 48-hour delivery ended the day quoted at BRL1.1789/1.1790, compared to Tuesday's BRL1.1760. \par \par \uc2  Early in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the real/dollar mini-band at BRL1.1715-1.1815, up 0.10 centavos from the BRL1.1705-1.1805 previously. \par \par \uc2  Government institutions spent part of the day selling dollars at BRL1.1790 "but then the market began to sell at BRL1.1789," a trader said. "The market was overbought." \par \par \uc2  -By Geraldo Samor; 55-21-580-9394; gsamor@ap.org \par 