\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real ends flat amid reported  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 1998\par 22:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Sept 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended flat at 1.1780 to the dollar in the commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday amid reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Banco do Brasil  was seen selling dollars in the market on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to prevent the real from weakening. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials would not confirm the reported dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was estimated to have sold between $600 million and $1.0 billion amid huge net outflows of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1715 local/1815 GMT on Friday, preliminary figures for commercial and financial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts showed a $1.1 billion deficit and dealers said it might turn into a larger deficit at the end of the day when all transactions were registered. \par \par \uc2  Brazil had already seen a $3.81 billion net outflow from the commercial and floating exchange rate markets in the first three days of September, extending the sharp losses seen in August, dealers said Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the floating interbank rate market, the real closed at 1.1810 per greenback, down 0.01 percent in the day. In the parallel market, the real the closed at 1.270 per dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  ((Carlos Sbarai, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5413)). \par \par \