\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil shrs set for quiet day with some buy-backs. \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Sept 4 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks are poised for a quiet session on Friday, with some investors buying back on Thursday's steep price losses, but most players are likely to stay away from the market ahead of Monday's holiday. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody would take up a risky position today, ahead of Monday's holiday," said a trader at Banco Santander in Sao Paulo. "It will be a quiet day with very little volume." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday, the bourse's key Bovespa index\tab    plunged 8.61 percent to close at 6,219 points, or at its two-year low, after Moody's Investors Service downgraded the country's speculative credit rating.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Yesterday's fall was definitely exaggerated," said another trader at big local bank, expecting a decent price correction on Friday. Moody's said Thursday it was downgrading its ceiling for Brazilian foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds and notes to B2 from B1 and the ceiling for foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bank deposits to Caa1.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The local stock market reacted immediately to the news. However, Brazil's dollar-denominated debt, namely C-bonds, traded in New York, seemed to weather the effect. The papers were trading up 1.750 points at 56.625 on early Friday. In the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the real was trading down 0.04 percent at 1.1785 to the dollar in early trade.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders said the market was nervous after the real dipped 0.08 percent on Thursday and that sentiment would still depend largely on fresh developments on Russia's economic situation and the knock-on effect it may have on other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was rumoured to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market Thursday selling dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bluechip activity Thursday:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Telebras  down 10.29 pct at 76.70 reais\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Petrobras  down 5 pct at 133 reais\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Eletrobras  down 8.41 pct at 18.60 reais\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Vale do Rio Doce  down 8.88 pct at 15.40 reais.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bovespa :* Thursday: down 8.61 pct at 6,219 points\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Week: down 7.8 pct * Month: down 3.9 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Year-to-date: down 39.0 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SELIC (open): 2.09 pct, Dollar/Real: 1.1785 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Noriko Yamaguchi, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5423)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9400rrk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
