\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Cenbank seen  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  markets. \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 22:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Sept 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in late trade Thursday in a bid to calm nervous investors amid a global economic fears, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bank was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-owned Banco do Brasil, selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 1.1780 to the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not comment on the reported dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  The real opened at 1.1780 to the dollar, or 0.08 percent lower than Wednesday's close, and stayed hovering around that level for most of the day until the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly stepped in to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling further. \par \par \uc2  The real was still trading at 1.1780 by 1655 local/1955 GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was suffering a large net outflow of dollars amid an escalating crisis. \par \par \uc2  "The continuous outflow of dollars is scary. And news that Moody's cut its credit rating on Brazilian debt fell like a bomb on the market," one local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service said it downgraded its credit ratings on the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt to B2 from B1. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was practically no expectation for a dollar inflow in the market under the current situation. \par \par \uc2  In the local futures market, October dollar contracts were trading up 0.16 percent, while November contracts were trading up 0.21 percent, meaning the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value was seen rising more in the near future. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The local bourse was also reflecting the nervousness in Brazilian markets. The key Bovespa index\tab    was down 8.45 percent at 6,230 points shortly before the session's close.\par Brazil's dollar-denominated C-bonds\tab \tab   traded in New York, was down 0.750 points at 54.75 at 1700 local/1800 gmt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5423, noriko.yamaguchi@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9300qqd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
